{#- Notification of a security compromise (POPIA section 22). English template shipped with Tripline Scope.
    Hospitals add translations as templates/notices/<language>/notice.md.j2 (same variables), and may override a
    single exposure combination with templates/notices/<language>/<combination>.md.j2.
    Merge fields in «guillemets» are filled by the hospital's mail-merge or SMS system from people.csv. -#}
# Notice of a security compromise affecting your personal information

{% if audience == "guardian" -%}
Dear parent or guardian of «first_name» «last_name»,

We are writing to you because you are recorded as the parent or guardian of «first_name», who is under 18.
{%- else -%}
Dear «first_name» «last_name»,
{%- endif %}

Reference: «person_ref»

## What happened and when

Between {{ incident_start }} and {{ incident_end }}, {{ hospital_name }} became aware that an unauthorised person
gained access to systems that hold patient records. {% if consequence == "confirmed_copy" -%}
We have confirmed that a copy of some information about {{ "your child" if audience == "guardian" else "you" }} was
obtained by an unauthorised party.
{%- elif consequence == "access_observed" -%}
Our investigation shows that the records containing information about {{ "your child" if audience == "guardian" else "you" }}
were accessed. We have not confirmed that the information was copied.
{%- else -%}
The records containing information about {{ "your child" if audience == "guardian" else "you" }} may have been accessed.
We have no evidence at this stage that the information was copied, but we cannot rule it out.
{%- endif %}

The information involved:
{% for c in categories %}
- {{ c.label }}
{%- endfor %}

## What we are doing

{% for m in measures -%}
- {{ m }}
{% endfor %}
## What you can do

{% for c in categories if c.advice -%}
- {{ c.advice }}
{% endfor -%}
- Be careful of phone calls, SMS or e-mail messages that mention this incident or ask for passwords, PINs or payments.
  {{ hospital_name }} will never ask you for your banking PIN or passwords.

## Who accessed the information

{{ accessed_by }}

## Contact us

{{ contact }}

You may also lodge a complaint with the Information Regulator (South Africa).
